# Catalog Data and JS Rules

- Keep `js/data.js` as the single source of truth for catalog entities.
- Define stable object shape for each item (id, title, price model, status, tags, media).
- Never depend on display order only; use explicit sort keys where needed.
- Keep filtering deterministic and composable (search + category + status + sort).
- Preserve URL/share state for filters when practical.
- Handle empty, error, and loading states explicitly in rendering logic.

## Safety and Maintainability

- Do not mutate source arrays in-place during filtering/sorting.
- Escape or sanitize user-facing dynamic HTML content before injection.
- Keep page-specific logic isolated (`catalog.js` vs `case-page.js`).
